      "worked": "Let $D_f$ be the domain of $f$. The natural domain of $g$ is $D_g=\\{x:x\\in D_f\\text{ and }-x\\in D_f\\}$, which is symmetric about $0$.\n\nFor every $x\\in D_g$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\ng(-x)&=f(-x)f(x)\\\\\ng(-x)&=f(x)f(-x)\\\\\ng(-x)&=g(x).\n\\end{align*}$$\nThus $g$ is even wherever the product defines a function. It is also odd if it is identically zero.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
